      "writtenOn": "2019-03-27T20:52:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "is this the state timeout (what loop)?\n\nAlso, I have seen states existing at different times if different conditions are met. Can we make timeouts with conditions that are run instead?\n\nHere is an example: https://chromium.git.corp.google.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/840eb397d38ba49a905955943d74b41160dfdd68/common/usb_pd_protocol.c#2978",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "4056dc38c0a6097587ad0dfa55850dc7530a383d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c1146d0e_780d774a",
        "filename": "include/usb_tc_sm.h",
        "patchSetId": 59
      },
      "lineNbr": 77,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-01T19:38:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This sets the state machine loop timeout value. Each state that deals with a particular conditional timeout does so as follows: using cc_debounce as an example:\ntc[port].cc_debounce \u003d get_time().val + PD_T_CC_DEBOUNCE;\n\nThen each loop of the state machine in the particular state would:\nif (get_time().val \u003c tc[port].cc_debounce)",
      "parentUuid": "0bc26ddd_4a45d6f7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "4056dc38c0a6097587ad0dfa55850dc7530a383d",
