      "writtenOn": "2019-03-27T20:52:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this seems like an appropriate place to describe (very briefly) what the support timer is used for and why the code cares.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 81,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 84,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "4056dc38c0a6097587ad0dfa55850dc7530a383d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2dd759fa_12e7ae4e",
        "filename": "include/usb_tc_sm.h",
        "patchSetId": 59
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-01T19:38:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the spec.\n\nA Charge-Through VCONN-Powered USB Device shall start a Charge-Through Support Timer when it\nenters the Attached.SNK state. If a Charge-Through VCONN-Powered USB Device fails to exit the\nAttached.SNK state before the Charge-Through Support Timer exceeds tAMETimeout, it shall\npresent a USB Billboard Device Class interface indicating that it does not support Charge-Through.\n\nI think it\u0027ll get untenable to try and define USB Type-C/PD terms and acronyms. The spec. should be consulted for the definitions.",
      "parentUuid": "0b6fc6d0_c48fcefa",
